sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant I as Interviewer
    participant C as Candidate
    participant B as Whiteboard
    I->>C: design this system
    C->>I: clarify scope, users, and what "works" means
    C->>B: functional and non-functional requirements
    C->>B: SLIs and SLO targets — the contract
    C->>I: confirm the numbers before drawing anything
    C->>B: capacity estimates — QPS, storage, bandwidth
    C->>B: high-level architecture, data flow first
    I->>C: push on one component
    C->>B: deep dive — data model, partitioning, hot paths
    C->>B: failure modes and blast radius
    C->>B: what you would monitor, and what pages a human
    Note over C: requirements to SLOs to numbers to architecture — never start at the boxes
